# MCP Knowledge & Changing Interfaces

## Knowledge Providers
- **Archon MCP**: query architecture decisions, historical context, and implementation guidelines instead of speculating.
- **Serena MCP**: retrieve project-level briefs, workflows, and recent updates specific to GoMake services.
- **MUI MCP**: confirm component usage patterns, theming knobs, and accessibility considerations for Material-UI.

Always check these providers first when requirements or patterns are unclear; their responses are the canonical source of truth.

## Dynamic Backend Contracts
- Treat REST endpoints, Socket.IO events, and TypeScript interfaces as volatile—cross-check the latest code under `src/services/**`, `src/widgets/frontdesk/**`, and generated types before coding against them.
- When integrating with APIs, inspect `frontdesk` endpoint definitions and recent commits to catch renamed paths or payload tweaks.
- For sockets, review `messaging-service.ts` and backend specs; log unexpected payloads and fail gracefully when shapes diverge.

## Implementation Checklist
- Validate assumptions made from older docs by re-querying MCP knowledge bases; document any detected drift.
- Gate feature flags or experimental endpoints behind configuration checks so the UI tolerates backend changes.
- Keep error handling defensive—surface informative messages when endpoints or contracts shift unexpectedly.
